# Disposable-DB Verification, Migration States, and DevOps Handoff Packet

<!-- GEN: Why: proves the migration on a throwaway database with data, enforces the 3-tier authority model, and equips DevOps with a complete Changes + Reasons + Per-Environment (develop/staging/production) Schema & Data Runbook. Kind: Mandatory. -->

> Topic: Disposable-DB verification checks (`V1`–`V8`), migration states, the mandatory DevOps Migration Handoff Packet (`develop` / `staging` / `production` schema & data runbook), and `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR` review grading (`M9`–`M12`).

Rules **M2**, **M9**, **M10**, **M11**, and **M12**.

---

## 1. Disposable-DB Verification Recipe (`V1`–`V8`, `M9`)

Execute all 8 checks against a **local/disposable database** (`{{local_selector}}`) before marking a task done or migrating `develop`:

| # | Check | Command / Query | Pass Criteria (`PASS` / `FAIL`) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **V1** | **Clean Install from Zero** | `{{clean_install_cmd}}` | `PASS` when entire chain applies from empty DB to head (`exit 0`) |
| **V2** | **Single Head & Zero Drift** | `{{heads_and_drift_cmd}}` | `PASS` when 1 head exists and zero model/schema drift is detected |
| **V3** | **Upgrade Over Seeded Data** | Step back (`downgrade -1`) → seed multi-tenant rows, `NULL`s, & edge cases → `upgrade head` | `PASS` when upgrade succeeds on realistic existing rows |
| **V4** | **Data Backfill Invariants (`B7`)** | Run invariant SQL (`SELECT count(*) ... WHERE <unmigrated> = 0`) & cross-tenant isolation check | `PASS` when unmigrated count is `0` and other tenants' rows are untouched |
| **V5** | **Reversibility (`downgrade` / `upgrade`)** | `{{reversibility_cmd}}` | `PASS` when `downgrade -1` and re-`upgrade head` both exit `0` |
| **V6** | **Valid Indexes Check** | `{{invalid_index_query}}` | `PASS` when `0` invalid indexes exist |
| **V7** | **Offline SQL & Lock Review** | `{{offline_sql_cmd}}` | `PASS` when generated SQL includes `lock_timeout` and matches safe patterns |
| **V8** | **Automated Migration & API Tests** | `{{migration_test_cmd}}` | `PASS` when migration test suite and affected service/API tests exit `0` |

