## 2. Canonical Migration States (`M11`)

Record the migration state alongside the core gate status (`PASS` / `FAIL` / `BLOCKED` / `NOT_RUN`):

| Migration State | Set By | Meaning & Required Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| `NOT_REQUIRED` | Agent | Task touches no schema or stored data (`drift_check_cmd` is clean) |
| `PENDING` | Agent | Revision written and `V1`–`V8` verified `PASS` on disposable DB; not applied to shared DBs |
| `READY_FOR_HANDOFF` | Agent | `PENDING` + `migration-handoff.md` is complete for the user / DevOps |
| `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED` | User / DevOps (or Agent on `develop` when explicitly requested by user) | Migration applied to named target (`develop` / `staging` / `production`), postchecks pending |
| `VERIFIED_IN_TARGET` | User / DevOps (or Agent on `develop` when explicitly requested by user) | Migration + data backfill + postchecks verified `PASS` on the named target |
| `FAILED` | Agent / User / DevOps | Migration or postcheck failed; records failing step, error, and recovery action taken |

