## 4. Review Severity Rubric (`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`)

| Severity | Database Migration Findings |
|---|---|
| **`BLOCKER`** | • Agent running migrations on `staging` or `production`, or on `develop` without explicit user request (**M2**)<br>• Delivering schema changes via `create_all()`, `db push`, `reset`, or manual SQL outside revisions (**M3**)<br>• Editing an already-deployed revision, leaving multiple Alembic/migration heads, or importing live app ORM models inside a revision (**M5**)<br>• Destructive drop/rename/type-change in the same phase as running code (`Expand → Contract` violated) or unguarded table rewrite / non-concurrent index build on a populated table (**M4, M6, M7**)<br>• Unscoped or unbatched data backfill, string-interpolated SQL, or secret/PII leaked in revision or handoff packet (**M8, M14**)<br>• Missing `V1`–`V8` disposable-DB verification or missing `migration-handoff.md` (**M9, M12**) |
| **`MAJOR`** | • Missing `SET LOCAL lock_timeout` on DDL touching existing tables (**M7**)<br>• Missing or fake `downgrade()` without an explicit irreversible-data note and backup recovery procedure (**M5, M10**)<br>• Handoff packet missing the **Changes & Reasons** table or missing the **Data Backfill / Postcheck commands** for `develop`, `staging`, and `production` (**M12**) |
| **`MINOR`** | • Non-imperative revision message slug or minor formatting inconsistency in `migration-handoff.md` |
